1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,188
What if every post you scrolled past

2
00:00:02,208 --> 00:00:03,151
was a market,

3
00:00:03,171 --> 00:00:04,277
and you could own a piece of

4
00:00:04,297 --> 00:00:05,012
it?

5
00:00:05,762 --> 00:00:07,382
We build for creators.

6
00:00:07,457 --> 00:00:08,946
We've watched them do the work while

7
00:00:08,966 --> 00:00:10,502
platforms keep the money,

8
00:00:10,522 --> 00:00:11,826
and we want the people who make

9
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:13,590
the posts, and the fans who find

10
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:15,564
them early, to share in what they

11
00:00:15,584 --> 00:00:16,647
create.

12
00:00:17,397 --> 00:00:19,339
Today a creator earns a sliver of

13
00:00:19,359 --> 00:00:22,210
ad revenue, and early fans get nothing.

14
00:00:22,563 --> 00:00:24,262
Creator coins exist,

15
00:00:24,282 --> 00:00:26,331
but they die on their curve.

16
00:00:27,081 --> 00:00:28,701
Monad changes that.

17
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:30,707
Blocks every three hundred milliseconds,

18
00:00:30,727 --> 00:00:32,413
final in about half a second,

19
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:34,053
for a fraction of a cent.

20
00:00:34,186 --> 00:00:35,699
Fast enough to put a market under

21
00:00:35,719 --> 00:00:36,991
every post.

22
00:00:37,741 --> 00:00:39,486
Juno does three things.

23
00:00:39,506 --> 00:00:42,481
Post: a photo becomes its own coin.

24
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:44,292
Buy: one tap,

25
00:00:44,312 --> 00:00:45,735
straight from the feed.

26
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:47,810
Graduate: when a curve fills,

27
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:50,074
the post opens its own Kuru order

28
00:00:50,094 --> 00:00:50,948
book.

29
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:53,988
And it's live on Monad testnet.

30
00:00:54,008 --> 00:00:56,252
A buy executed in four hundred sixteen

31
00:00:56,272 --> 00:00:59,492
milliseconds. A post graduated into Kuru.

32
00:00:59,512 --> 00:01:00,711
Perps on Perpl,

33
00:01:00,731 --> 00:01:03,198
and a Chainlink CRE attestation.

34
00:01:03,273 --> 00:01:05,462
Each one a real transaction.

35
00:01:06,212 --> 00:01:07,504
It's for creators,

36
00:01:07,524 --> 00:01:09,655
and the fans who find them first.

37
00:01:10,008 --> 00:01:12,125
Every receipt is a card they share,

38
00:01:12,145 --> 00:01:14,574
and every graduation lists a new market

39
00:01:14,594 --> 00:01:15,796
on Kuru.

40
00:01:16,546 --> 00:01:19,118
Juno. Every post is a market.
